                <pb facs="0846" n="747" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg747"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.52/132: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Third Secretary of Embassy in Spain</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Wendelin</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-10-23T17:00:00+00:00">October 23, 1936—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>X–239. In view of serious situation and present indications Embassy will again be
                    opened as place of refuge. Military Attaché has been placed in charge of
                    important matters in connection therewith, for which he is qualified. Please
                    inform War.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wendelin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
